      "content": "I understand wanting to get it right the first time — waking a sick baby repeatedly is exhausting. But I'd stick with 3.75mL rather than going higher based on a forum: 10-15mg/kg is the standard range, and 3.75mL (120mg) puts him right in that safe zone. More Tylenol doesn't mean better fever control, and exceeding recommended doses risks liver strain, which is the real danger with acetaminophen. If the fever isn't controlled on a proper dose, that's a reason to call his pediatrician, not to increase the amount on your own.",
